lines=['# One year with 32 different fictional customers','',f"**32 customers, 32 starting professions, all 20 profession categories, all 25 vocations, {len(j['coverage']['classesUsed'])} classes used, and 35 annual scenarios.** Three scenarios are matched alternatives for existing customers, not additional people. The app processed **{n(j['accountDays'])} account-days** and **{n(j['totals']['requests'])} completed requests**.",'','The app supports much more than the original Analyst/Networking use case. Its career trees and retained histories work across healthcare, teaching, trades, farming, law, logistics, creative work, service and other fields. The main problems are progression clarity, a confirmed Network Weaver scope defect, uneven rewards for different schedules, and limited later career-skill spending.','', '**These are fictional profiles and scripted work/exam inputs run through the app’s real domain functions. They are not customer interviews, retention measurements, predicted fitness gains or evidence of professional competence.** The interpretation of each experience is a hypothesis grounded in its trace.','', '[All complete profiles in one document](CUSTOMERS.md) · [Methods and assumptions](METHOD.md) · [Priority findings](PRIORITIES.md) · [Raw summary CSV](summary.csv) · [Day 7/30/90/180/365 checkpoints](checkpoints.csv)','', '## At a glance','',f"- All eight Basic classes and Monk were used at registration. Later paths brought observed class coverage to **{len(j['coverage']['classesUsed'])} of {len(classes)}** definitions; all 20 category-specific career tools became available somewhere in the cohort.",f"- **{j['totals']['primaryPrestigeUsers']} of 32** primary profiles entered a prestige class; first entries ranged from day **{min(prestige)} to {max(prestige)}**. No Ascendant entry was chosen in these routines. Tomas qualifies to take World Forger’s trial, and Felix/Darius qualify for Phantom’s trial; those were beyond their declared goals.",f"- **{len(gold)} of 32** reached A/Gold within the year, between days **{min(gold)} and {max(gold)}**. Median among those achievers was **{stats.median(gold):.0f} days**. The other 20 did not reach A; this is not a cohort-wide nine-to-twelve-month forecast.",f"- Player levels ended at **{min(r['final']['playerLevel'] for r in primary)}–{max(r['final']['playerLevel'] for r in primary)}**; profession levels at **{min(r['final']['professionLevel'] for r in primary)}–{max(r['final']['professionLevel'] for r in primary)}**. Vocation levels were **{min(r['final']['vocationLevel'] for r in primary)}–{max(r['final']['vocationLevel'] for r in primary)}** and are not exam-gated.",f"- All **{n(j['totals']['battles'])} ordinary encounter attempts** were won with the shared policy, learned builds, actual purchases and available companions. This is evidence of accessible ordinary progression in these scenarios, not Elite-hunt balance or class equality.",f"- **{j['totals']['expiredCommitments']} accepted commitments expired** across the 35 runs. Earned XP and earlier histories were retained. There were **{j['totals']['duplicateGuards']} rejected duplicate reward attempts**, no combat action-bound cases, and daily gold reconciliation passed.",'','![Year-end levels and rewards for every customer](cohort.png)','', '## The customers','', 'Each linked profile includes backstory, goals, constraints, equipment, schedule, concrete career work, five checkpoints, retained class/profession history, stats, skills, Adventure outcomes and an experience assessment. Paige and Elena change careers; the year-end numbers describe their current tracks, while their earlier roles remain in the profile history.','', '| Customer / age | Starting profession → vocation | Starting → year-end class | Player / class / profession / vocation levels | Rank |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
